1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,454
Jane is a planet surfer.

2
00:00:01,637 --> 00:00:03,660
She loves exploring our blue marble.

3
00:00:03,901 --> 00:00:07,294
Opinionated, well informed, and always monitoring the situation.

4
00:00:07,697 --> 00:00:09,674
We call her a Superpredictor.

5
00:00:10,124 --> 00:00:15,131
On a typical day, Jane opens Urban Game Theory and scrolls the latest proposals.

6
00:00:15,314 --> 00:00:17,836
A new apartment block in Zagreb catches her eye.

7
00:00:17,961 --> 00:00:19,008
She clicks.

8
00:00:19,458 --> 00:00:21,678
The three-dimensional view brings it to life.

9
00:00:21,861 --> 00:00:24,732
New homes, on these parcels, in this neighbourhood.

10
00:00:24,973 --> 00:00:26,078
It looks good.

11
00:00:26,319 --> 00:00:29,178
But Jane knows something the picture cannot tell her.

12
00:00:29,628 --> 00:00:34,518
In this example, the party promising to block the project is leading the next election.

13
00:00:35,131 --> 00:00:37,398
Jane thinks execution is unlikely.

14
00:00:37,581 --> 00:00:39,395
That suggests a NO bet.

15
00:00:39,845 --> 00:00:42,576
First, she checks who will resolve the outcome.

16
00:00:42,655 --> 00:00:44,271
Does she trust that lens?

17
00:00:44,512 --> 00:00:45,954
Then the details:

18
00:00:46,265 --> 00:00:51,597
money committed, pledges, donations, and parcel-owner acceptances.

19
00:00:52,001 --> 00:00:54,163
Every signal can change her view.

20
00:00:54,613 --> 00:00:56,113
Her conclusion holds.

21
00:00:56,517 --> 00:01:00,107
Jane selects NO, chooses her stake, and confirms.

22
00:01:00,348 --> 00:01:02,615
The stake stays locked until resolution.

23
00:01:03,112 --> 00:01:09,302
Cancellation or recorded expiry pays NO; execution pays YES.

24
00:01:09,752 --> 00:01:12,390
Then she spots another proposal nearby:

25
00:01:12,701 --> 00:01:15,293
buy two parcels and make a public park.

26
00:01:15,789 --> 00:01:17,115
Jane wants that to happen.

27
00:01:17,426 --> 00:01:20,447
She donates fifty dollars in devnet USDC.

28
00:01:20,897 --> 00:01:23,140
The donation sits in escrow.

29
00:01:23,265 --> 00:01:25,555
This plan needs all parcel owners to accept.

30
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:31,778
If it has not executed after a year, and expiry is recorded on-chain, Jane can claim her donation back.

31
00:01:32,228 --> 00:01:34,274
A forecast on one project.

32
00:01:34,399 --> 00:01:35,667
Support for another.

33
00:01:35,978 --> 00:01:38,605
Jane returns to happily surfing the planet.

34
00:01:38,846 --> 00:01:40,207
Urban Game Theory.

35
00:01:40,518 --> 00:01:45,338
Explore your world, predict what changes, and help shape what comes next.
